        "original_id": "fb4cd107-b69b-5b21-bfbe-3250d3e5338f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Manning Field at John L. Guidry Stadium\n- People: Eli Manning, Peyton Manning, Archie Manning, Philip Rivers\n- Organizations: New York Giants, San Diego Chargers, National Football League\n- Events: Manning Passing Academy, 2004 NFL Draft\n\nFacts:\n- Eli Manning was born on January 3, 1981.\n- Eli Manning is an American football quarterback for the New York Giants of the National Football League.\n- In the 2004 NFL Draft, the San Diego Chargers drafted Eli Manning with the first overall pick.\n- Eli Manning was immediately traded from the San Diego Chargers to the New York Giants in a deal highlighted by the fourth overall selection, Philip Rivers.\n- The playing surface at Manning Field at John L. Guidry Stadium is named Manning Field after the Manning family.\n- Peyton Manning, Eli Manning, and Archie Manning hold the Manning Passing Academy football camp at Manning Field at John L. Guidry Stadium.",
